## Existing Code Policy

This is **not a backend rewrite project**. Before any change, classify every component:

| Class | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `REUSE AS-IS` | Working, keep |
| `REUSE WITH ADAPTER` | Working engine, adapt surface |
| `TURKEY UI REBUILD` | Rebuild Turkey UX only |
| `INTERNATIONAL ONLY` | Do not touch |
| `LEGACY / REMOVE AFTER VALIDATION` | Remove only after Turkey E2E passes |
| `SHARED ENGINE` | Used by both products |

**Working capability must not be deleted just because it was written in an old sprint.**

---

## Turkey Frontend Rebuild Policy

New Turkey implementation must:
- Use the shared engine
- NOT modify the International product
- Be based on organisation segmentation
- Use Turkey-specific information architecture
- NOT replace International chrome via generic `Role.BUYER` conditions

`hide ≠ delete` — sourcing capabilities stay in the backend for future commercial activation.

---

## Migration Strategy (Ordered)

1. Production backup → 2. Git immutable tag → 3. Database backup → 4. Turkey capability inventory → 5. International baseline screenshots/tests → 6. Turkey Master Specification freeze → 7. Clean Turkey product shell → 8. Existing engine adapters → 9. Turkey journeys → 10. Turkey E2E testing → 11. International regression → 12. Security/tenant regression → 13. Production deployment → 14. Production acceptance → 15. Legacy cleanup

**Old Turkey implementation must not be deleted until the replacement passes E2E acceptance, International non-regression, tenant-isolation tests, and production acceptance.**
